course: dictionary
lesson: 3915
title: Frogfish: a fish that hides in plain sight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A frogfish is a small, lumpy sea fish that lives in warm oceans, often among coral reefs. It is a kind of anglerfish, so it has a lure on its head to catch food. «The frogfish looks like a sponge or rock, waits for fish and swallows them quickly.» The sentence tells you it is good at hiding and at catching its food.
explain: Most fish swim, but a frogfish walks along the sea floor. It uses its fins like legs. Walking slowly over the sea floor helps it stay close to the rocks and sponges it looks like.
explain: Prey means an animal that another animal hunts for food. «Even fish as big as itself» means a frogfish can swallow prey as big as its own body. Check this by swapping in your own meaning: does «a frogfish can swallow fish as big as its own body» still make sense? It does, so you have understood the clue.
fact: A frogfish is a small, lumpy sea fish.
fact: A frogfish is a kind of anglerfish.
fact: Frogfish live in warm oceans, often on coral reefs.
fact: Camouflage means hiding by looking like your surroundings, such as a rock or sponge.
fact: A frogfish uses a lure on its head to catch prey.
exercise: «The frogfish looks like a sponge or rock.» What is a frogfish? | A kind of coral that grows in warm seas | A furry animal from the forest | *A small, lumpy sea fish | A large bird that nests on cliffs
exercise: A frogfish moves along the sea floor. What does it use its fins for? | *Walking, like legs | Singing to other fish | Flying | Digging holes in the sand
exercise: What is camouflage, and how does a frogfish use it? | *Looking like a rock or sponge to hide | Eating plants on the reef | Glowing to scare other fish | Swimming very fast to escape
test:
«The frogfish swallows fish as big as itself.» What does this mean? | It eats only tiny plankton | It cannot eat at all | *It can swallow prey as big as its own body | It only drinks water
test:
What does the lure on a frogfish's head help it do? | Breathe underwater | *Catch prey | Keep warm | Swim faster
exam:
Why might a frogfish look like a sponge or rock? | To fly over the reef | To attract other frogfish with songs | *To hide and wait for prey | To keep dry in the sun
